#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Colourised network topology map for the lab-view walkthrough.

ACTIVITY-AWARE: the diagram is chosen per activity from the MAPS registry below.
lab-view.zsh calls:  python3 network_map.py <COLS> <ROWS> <ACTIVITY>
(ACTIVITY is one of: 1 2.1 2.2 3 4.1 4.2 ; falls back to "1" if unknown.)

HOW TO ADD A PER-WEEK MAP
-------------------------
1. Paste that week's diagram as a raw string (like MAP_DMZ below).
2. Register it:      MAPS["2.2"] = MAP_DNS
3. Colour overlay:   by default every activity reuses draw_dmz() (the bespoke
   overlay whose coordinates match MAP_DMZ). When you give an activity a DIFFERENT
   map, its coordinates won't match draw_dmz — so also point it at the generic
   auto-colouriser (borders white, IPv4 violet, IPv6 blue):
       DRAWS["2.2"] = draw_generic
   ...or write a bespoke draw_<activity>(cv) and register that instead.

Canvas helpers (0-indexed, inclusive):
    cv.fill(r0,r1,c0,c1,colour)              rectangle background
    cv.box_draw(r0,r1,c0,c1,fill,border)     filled box (border = text colour)
    cv.line(r0,r1,c0,c1,colour)              colour box-drawing chars only
    cv.ink(r0,r1,c0,c1,colour[,only_lines])  colour text
    cv.label(r0,r1,c0,c1,colour[,bg])        colour text (+ optional bg)

Routing colours: violet=IPv4, blue=IPv6, cyan=IPv6-over-IPv4 tunnel, white=other.
"""
